+## GLM prefill lanes and FP8 wire rows (TF_GLM_PREFILL_LANES, TF_GLM_WIRE_FP8)
+
+Hugh Madden ([@dangerm00se](https://x.com/dangerm00se), [hughmadden](https://github.com/hughmadden)) authored the
+prefill lanes and the FP8 wire rows of the AFD design that `families/glm5_next/cuda/prefill_pairs.py`'s
+`run_lanes` / `_forward_lanes` / `lane_buffers` and `wire_fp8.py` bring to this tree's attention/expert split:
+the two-lane prefill of whole prompt chunks in [mimo26f-afd](https://github.com/hughmadden/mimo26f-afd/tree/bab9fa2f2fc1e22ae67b56fbc1c209278f6a9d79)
+(`crates/mimo26-coordinator/src/dforward.rs`), the prefill in up to four lanes (four lanes of 2,048 rows by default,
+the exchanges in flight bounded by the expert backend's depth) and the FP8 E4M3 wire rows with a UE8M0 scale per 32
+values (`Fp8E4m3Ue8m0K32`: `crates/glm53f-coordinator/kernels/wire.cu`, `src/wire.rs`, `src/fp8.rs`, from mimo26f-afd's
+`crates/mimo26-coordinator/kernels/glue.cu`, `crates/mimo26-attn/kernels/include/mimo26_attn_device.cuh`,
+`crates/mimo26-attn/kernels/kv_cache_fp8.cu` and `crates/mimo26-load/src/e4m3.rs`) in
+[glm53f-afd](https://github.com/hughmadden/glm53f-afd/tree/91db3cc6fe672e2724efa3464f63bd31493f63f6)
+(`crates/glm53f-forward/src/forward.rs` `run_lanes`, `src/experts.rs` `ExpertBackend::depth`), MIT License, Copyright
+(c) 2026 Turquoise Bay AI Pty Ltd (the MIT text above). The wire row format is DS41RT's, by T.J. Purtell
+([@wrldsuksgo2mars](https://x.com/wrldsuksgo2mars), [tpurtell/ds41rt](https://github.com/tpurtell/ds41rt), MIT),
+carried through mimo26f-afd. No code is copied: the lanes are written for this tree's whole prompt chunks over the
+MCDMA wire (one exchange in flight per link, so the lanes go in lane order and a lane's attention runs inside the
+exchange windows of the lanes before it); the codec is torch operations and a table of every bf16 magnitude's code
+computed with a plain-Python transcription of glm53f-afd's device encoder, and the tests check it byte for byte
+against that transcription. Both are off unless set: `TF_GLM_PREFILL_LANES` (1 .. 4; unset follows
+`TF_GLM_PREFILL_PAIRS`, 2 being this tree's pairs) and `TF_GLM_WIRE_FP8=1` (which changes the experts' inputs).
